WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.080
This isn’t the standard
YouTuber burnout-apology video.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.840
And it’s not “oh, woe is me,
I’m leaving forever”.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.720
I’m going somewhere with this.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:08.680
Literally.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.520
I’ve been throwing stuff
at the internet since 1999.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.160
And for many, many years,
that stuff went almost nowhere.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.840
I had occasional bits of success,

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.320
but could never make
any of them last long-term.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.240
I remember thinking, so many times
during all those years…

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.520
will any of this
stuff I’m making ever work?

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.720
Well, this did.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.080
I didn’t know that,
back when I was filming

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.360
the first videos for the series
that was then called

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.880
Things You Might Not Know,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.040
I just held out my phone
at arm’s length

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.720
and talked into it for 90 seconds
with almost no research!

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.360
I really don’t like
those videos now.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.120
But the first of them
was published

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.920
exactly ten years
before this one.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.680
To the minute.
4pm, January 1st, 2014.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.240
For the first month
of that format,

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.240
I was publishing a video
almost every day,

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.320
and then I settled down:
one video a week.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.880
Mostly on location,
near windswept infrastructure,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.160
although there’s computer science
and linguistics in there too,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.560
and occasional green-screen
animated videos.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.600
I experimented with
other formats on other days,

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.640
but the rule
I set myself was:

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.720
Monday, 4pm,
something interesting.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.160
I never got to space.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.680
I never got to
the ocean depths.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.760
And I never got to fly harnessed
underneath a helicopter,

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.760
I couldn’t find an excuse
to do that one.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.240
But I never missed a week.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.880
There’s been a few guest videos,
of course,

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.960
and occasionally some
blatant filler.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.440
One time I just uploaded
two and a half hours of

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:30.120
unedited footage of garlic bread
flying to the edge of space,

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.040
and that turned into one of the
most viewed videos I’ve ever had.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.520
Sometimes a video would be
a day or two early or late

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.640
for one reason or another.
But to my own satisfaction,

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.280
which is ultimately the
only thing that I’m counting,

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.040
there’s been a video a week
for ten years.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.040
I never broke the streak.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.280
I don’t know when I decided
to try for ten years.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.440
It felt like a
good, round number to reach.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.320
As the YouTube game
changed over the years,

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.800
as the channel became bigger,

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.600
as my own standards
became higher and higher

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.200
to keep pace with all the people

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.080
I was collaborating with
and competing with,

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.280
as this became my life–

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.840
I decided that my goal
was ten years.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.280
And that is today,
as this is published.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.640
4pm, January 1st, 2024.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:16.560
So now it’s time
to take a breather.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.400
I can’t keep this up.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.920
This is my dream job, and
I have a lot of fun doing it.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.600
I know I’m incredibly lucky.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.240
But a dream job is still a job.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.000
And it’s a job that keeps getting
bigger and more complicated

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.720
and I am so tired!

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.280
There’s nothing in my life
right now except work.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.520
I did get close to burning out,

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.040
but fortunately I always knew
when to step back from the brink.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.880
And it’s not like I can
drop the quality back down?

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.800
That’s not how YouTube
works these days.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.040
Over the last year or so,
I have talked to some folks

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.720
who are more successful than me,

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.160
who were in this position
a few years back.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.480
And it’s clear that I now
have two possible choices.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.240
I could keep making
bigger and better things,

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.480
keep climbing the ladder,

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.640
build a business,
hire full-time employees…

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.120
and end up as a manager.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.160
And that would be great for
someone who isn’t me,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.640
but I know I’m bad at that,

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.920
and I’d hate every second of it.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.040
So, option 2…
I could not do that,

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.400
I could do less,
and be happier.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.800
So I’m taking a break
for… some time.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.680
I don’t know when or
if I come back,

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:15.480
but when I do,
it won’t be weekly.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.360
At least, not in this format,
not here.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.680
This probably isn’t
goodbye-goodbye?

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:20.560
Like, not forever?

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.040
The podcast I host, Lateral,
is still going out weekly,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.240
my newsletter’s still going out,

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.400
the Plus channel will probably
return at some point,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.880
there’ll likely be new
Technical Difficulties episodes,

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.880
there are links to all those things
around here somewhere.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.440
And there will probably be
all-new projects here or somewhere else,

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.600
projects that are experimental
and weird and can fail.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.840
Because I miss doing
stuff like that.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.320
And when some fool comes along
and goes “oh, you fell off,

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.480
“this new stuff isn’t getting
the views is it?”…

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.160
Yeah. Okay. That’s fine.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.040
This project has worked,
and it’s time to move on.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.280
I’m still going to be looking for
interesting things to film here,

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.400
there’ll probably still be videos
here from time to time,

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.480
I really do love doing this.
There is a part of my brain

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.240
that desperately, desperately
does not want this to end.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.800
So if you’ve got an idea
for a future video,

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.960
you can still tell me about it.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:09.000
And one day, I might make it.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.000
But right now, I need to spend time
with people I hold dear,

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.200
I need there to be things in my life
that are not work,

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.000
and it’s been years
since that’s been true.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.600
I never celebrated
the milestones.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.200
Subscriber numbers
weren’t ever my goal.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.960
So I never did any big
so-many-subscribers thank you videos.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.640
But, still… thank you.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.400
To you watching, and to everyone
who’s helped along the way.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.760
I did think that
I should end this

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:34.200
with a big, syrupy, sentimental,
self-indulgent montage

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.000
and head off into the sunset…

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.640
…and you know what?

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:39.880
Just this once,

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.800
for the first time
in ten years…

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.000
that’s exactly what
I’m going to do.

